            "content": "# DeepSeek Agent - Fix Admin Edit Saving to MySQL (cPanel)\n\nThe application is running on cPanel with PHP + MySQL.\n\nCurrent problem:\n\nAdmin can edit data, but after refreshing the page the changes disappear or revert to the old values.\n\nFind the root cause and permanently fix it.\n\n## Step 1 - Trace the Complete Save Flow\n\nFor every editable module (Landing Page, Hero Section, Patients, Doctors, Settings, etc.), trace:\n\nReact Form\n\u2193\nonSubmit()\n\u2193\nMutation \/ API Call\n\u2193\nPHP Endpoint\n\u2193\nMySQL Query\n\u2193\nDatabase Commit\n\u2193\nFetch Updated Data\n\u2193\nUI Refresh\n\nIdentify where the save process fails.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 - Verify Frontend\n\nCheck that every Save button:\n\n* Calls the correct API.\n* Sends the correct JSON.\n* Waits for the API response.\n* Shows success only after the database update succeeds.\n* Refreshes React Query\/cache after saving.\n\nRemove any code that only updates local state or localStorage without saving to MySQL.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 - Verify PHP API\n\nFor every update endpoint:\n\n* Validate input.\n* Use PDO prepared statements.\n* Execute UPDATE queries.\n* Return JSON:\n  {\n  \"success\": true\n  }\n\nIf the update fails:\n\n* Return HTTP 500.\n* Log the real error to the PHP error log.\n* Return a generic error message to the client.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4 - Verify Database\n\nConfirm that:\n\n* UPDATE queries actually modify rows.\n* The correct primary key is used.\n* Transactions commit successfully.\n* No UPDATE query silently fails.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5 - Verify Data Reload\n\nAfter saving:\n\n* Reload the updated record from MySQL.\n* Refresh React Query cache.\n* Ensure the latest values appear after page refresh.\n* Ensure the latest values appear after logout\/login.\n* Ensure another browser sees the updated data.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6 - Landing Page Editing\n\nVerify that editing:\n\n* Hero Title\n* Hero Subtitle\n* About Section\n* Contact Information\n* Footer\n* Services\n* Testimonials\n\nupdates the MySQL database and remains after refreshing the page.\n\n---\n\n## Step 7 - Audit\n\nSearch the project for:\n\n* localStorage.setItem\n* localStorage.getItem\n* setState used as permanent storage\n* mock data\n* fake API\n* demo data\n\nReplace any remaining business-data storage with MySQL.\n\n---\n\n## Step 8 - Deliverables\n\nProvide:\n\n1. Root cause of the issue.\n2. Files modified.\n3. SQL queries used.\n4. API endpoints updated.\n5. Confirmation that edits now persist in MySQL after page refresh, logout\/login, and across different devices.",
