                    "text": "Now I have a thorough understanding of the architecture. Let me now plan the fix.\n\n## Complete Root Cause Analysis\n\n### The Problem\nThe application was built for the **Internet Computer (ICP)** blockchain, where data is stored in:\n1. **localStorage** (temporary local cache)\n2. **ICP Canister** (permanent blockchain storage)\n\nThe migration to PHP\/MySQL removed the ICP canister integration by setting the canister actor to `null`. However, **no PHP\/MySQL persistence was wired in to replace the ICP canister**.\n\n### What Happens When Admin Edits Data:\n\n**Landing Page Editing Flow:**\n1. User edits hero title, subtitle, etc. in the admin panel\n2. `saveFrontPageContentWithSync()` is called\n3. This function reads `siteConfig` and `doctorContentOverrides` from `localStorage`\n4. It tries to call `actor.saveFrontPageContent(serialized)` - **actor is null, so this fails**\n5. Falls back to `enqueueSync()` - **data goes to a sync queue in localStorage**\n6. Data NEVER reaches MySQL\n7. On page refresh, data is read from `localStorage` - IF localStorage is intact, changes appear\n8. If service worker triggers a reload, or localStorage is cleared, data reverts to defaults\n\n**Settings Editing Flow:**\n1. User edits settings (registry management)\n2. `saveRegistry()` \/ `savePatientRegistry()` is called\n3. These functions ONLY write to `localStorage`\n4. Data NEVER reaches MySQL\n5. No PHP `settings\/update.php` endpoint exists\n\n### The Missing Pieces:\n1. **No MySQL tables for landing page content** (hero section, services, testimonials, about, etc.)\n2. **No PHP endpoint to save landing page content** to MySQL\n3. **No PHP endpoint to update site settings** (only `get.php` exists)\n4. **Frontend never calls any PHP endpoint for saving** - it's all localStorage + ICP canister\n5. **`sync.php` is file-based JSON storage** - NOT MySQL, and NOT called by frontend\n\n### Fix Plan:\nSince we have compiled JS and can't rebuild the frontend, we need to:\n\n1. **Create MySQL tables for landing page content** (JSON storage in site_settings is ideal since the content is already JSON)\n2. **Create PHP endpoints**:\n   - `POST \/api\/landing\/save.php` - Save landing page content (siteConfig JSON to MySQL)\n   - `GET \/api\/landing\/get.php` - Load landing page content from MySQL\n   - `POST \/api\/settings\/update.php` - Update site settings\n3. **Modify the compiled JS** to call these PHP endpoints instead of (or in addition to) localStorage operations\n\nFor the JS modification, the key changes are:\n- In `saveFrontPageContentWithSync()` - add PHP API call to save the data\n- In `saveRegistry()` and `savePatientRegistry()` - add PHP API calls\n- When loading data - fetch from PHP API on initial load\n\nLet me now examine the exact JS code to modify. Since the JS is compiled (but not minified - I can see readable function names), I can make targeted edits.\n\nLet me look at the exact function signatures and the IDL definitions to understand what needs to change.\n\nActually, looking at the deployment report again, it says:\n> \"**`sync.php`** is kept for backward compatibility but is NOT used by the new system\"\n> \"**Frontend API client updated**\"\n> \"**React Query hooks migrated**\"\n> \"**Auth context migrated**\"\n\nThis suggests that the migration report claims the frontend was updated, but the compiled JS tells a different story - it's still using localStorage and ICP canister calls.\n\nSo the actual deployed state is:\n- Frontend: Still using localStorage + ICP canister (with canister = null)\n- PHP: Has endpoints but frontend doesn't call them\n- MySQL: Has schema but no data flows from frontend to MySQL\n\nLet me create a comprehensive fix plan:\n\n1. **Create landing page PHP API endpoints** (save\/get)\n2. **Create settings update PHP endpoint** \n3. **Modify compiled JS** to persist to PHP endpoints on save\n4. **Modify compiled JS** to fetch from PHP on load\n5. **Test the flow**\n\nLe